MARKET ANALYSIS · Bratislava new-builds · {asOfEn}

# The supply of Bratislava new-builds is growing and prices are not moving

The last two months on the Bratislava new-build market brought stronger sales, price stagnation and a further increase in the number of flats for sale. Sales rose from {qSalesThen} to {qSalesNow} flats against the previous period. The price level was unchanged, moving by {qPanelM2ChangePctEn}% on a comparable sample of projects. The supply of flats for sale rose to {qSupply}.

As of {asOfEn} the supply on the new-build market consisted, according to Residata's data, of {qSupply} flats across {qProjects} projects. On the sample of {qPanelProjects} projects we also track as of {qThenDateEn}, supply rose over the last {qPanelDays} days from {qPanelSupplyThen} to {qPanelSupplyNow} flats, that is by {qPanelSupplyChange} flats or {qPanelSupplyChangePctEn}%.

The average price of these flats on offer reached {qMeanM2} €/m² incl. VAT. On the comparable sample of projects it moved over the same period from {qPanelM2Then} to {qPanelM2Now} €/m² incl. VAT, a change of {qPanelM2ChangePctEn}%. It can be said that the prices of Bratislava new-builds are currently not moving, and that differences in the overall average are caused by the composition of supply rather than by movements in price lists.

The average absolute price of flats on offer stood at {qMeanPrice} € incl. VAT, while their average floor area reached {qMeanAreaEn} m².

